# Contiguous Memory Allocator for the aspeed-video capture buffers on the 64 MB
# AST2050. HW-VERIFIED NEED (2026-07-13): on real silicon the video engine binds,
# detects a live host VGA SIGNAL and mode-detects 1024x768 JPEG (sizeimage 512 KB),
# but VIDIOC_REQBUFS fails with ENOMEM -- vb2-dma-contig needs a physically
# contiguous 512 KB (order-7) buffer and the fragmented 64 MB box offers at most
# order-5 = 128 KB (per /proc/buddyinfo), with neither CMA nor compaction compiled
# in. CMA reserves a contiguous pool at boot that dma_alloc_coherent/vb2-dma-contig
# draw from; compaction/migration let the rest of the system defragment. This is the
# exact mainline-Aspeed approach (video_engine_memory), sized down for 64 MB.
#
# Pool size: default 16 MB (holds 3x512 KB buffers + the 24 KB JPEG header +
# alignment); override at boot with `cma=<N>M` on the kernel cmdline.
CONFIG_CMA=y
CONFIG_DMA_CMA=y
CONFIG_CMA_AREAS=7
CONFIG_CMA_SIZE_SEL_MBYTES=y
CONFIG_CMA_SIZE_MBYTES=16
CONFIG_DMA_CMA_ALIGNMENT=8
CONFIG_COMPACTION=y
CONFIG_MIGRATION=y
